      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# CI Diet\n\n[English](README.md) · [한국어](README.ko.md) · [简体中文](README.zh-Hans.md) · [हिन्दी](README.hi.md) · [Español](README.es.md) · [Français](README.fr.md)\n\n**Status:** alpha; `dsh-ci-diet@0.5.1` is on npm. The current source tree adds the **Settings → CI Diet Reports** review screen to the existing contracts, analysis and patch engines, CLI, DSH tools, Settings page, and self-contained HTML report. The review screen passed a real-browser E2E check in an earlier commit. The one-time defaults migration was verified separately in a DSH `0.2.1-rc.2` runtime with configEditor, SettingsForms, and Loader; it was not a new browser render. The DSH plugin now starts with preflight, history network access, and local apply enabled.\n\n**DSH defaults and migration.** New profiles enable `preflightEnabled`, `networkEnabled`, `localApplyEnabled` and CD001, CD002, CD004, CD006, CD008. The locked profile migration records `defaultsRevision: 2`. Profiles already migrated to revision 1 keep later switch and rule choices. State paths, retention, quotas, and existing numeric account inputs are preserved. CD003 and CD005 remain off unless enabled. Monetary estimates use both account inputs automatically; blank means unknown and explicit `0` is valid. Previously enabled billing keeps its zero defaults when a value was omitted.\n\nCI Diet finds GitHub Actions work that is likely wasted, preserves the evidence behind each finding, and previews small workflow edits for a human to review.\n\n**Installation alone does not save runner minutes.** Supported DSH deploy commands are checked automatically for savings candidates before running; workflow changes are applied only after review and approval. The DSH plugin has no approval, apply, or revert tools, and preflight itself never changes files. Its Settings pages store tool configuration and show the host's session-scoped reports and plans; they do not optimize a workflow. Approved local writes are enabled by default, but applying still requires a separate digest approval. There is no guarantee that any finding will reduce cost.\n\n`preflightEnabled` is on by default. Before a literal `git push`, `npm|pnpm|bun publish`, `wrangler deploy`, or `npm|pnpm|bun run deploy` in a supported stateless DSH bash tool (one with a `workdir` argument), CI Diet runs an offline check. It flags npm/pnpm CD006 candidates, a missing concurrency block in a PR-only workflow, and a Bun frozen install without an explicit download cache for review. When a candidate exists, the first command does not run; after the model reviews the items, retrying the same command is allowed. Preflight itself makes no network request and no automatic file change, and applying a plan still needs human approval. Persistent shells and complex shell wrappers cannot be identified reliably, so preflight skips them. Savings remain unmeasured, so no saving is claimed.\n\n## What it does\n\nThe static scan reads workflow YAML in a target checkout. The optional history sync uses read-only `gh api` calls to collect recent runs. Findings carry an evidence level (`observed`, `inferred`, or `static`) and per-axis collection coverage.\n\n| Rule | Finds | Possible plan |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| CD001 | PR runs made obsolete by a newer commit | `concurrency` edit |\n| CD002 | Overlapping triggers | explanation only |\n| CD003 | Heavy checks for docs-only changes | explanation only; off by default |\n| CD004 | Oversized matrices | explanation only |\n| CD005 | Jobs without `timeout-minutes` | timeout edit; off by default |\n| CD006 | npm / pnpm / Bun | [CD006](docs/spec/rules.md) |\n| CD008 | Long artifact retention | retention edit |\n\nCD001 helps overlapping superseded PR runs. CD005 caps abnormal runs; it does not reduce normal job runtime. CD008 changes artifact storage retention, not runner minutes. CD003 and CD005 remain off until their quality gates pass.\n\nCD006 also supports verified npm/pnpm setups and Bun jobs using `oven-sh/setup-bun@v2` followed by `bun install --frozen-lockfile` with a tracked text `bun.lock`. Bun adds a download-cache step; installation and tests still run. Cache restore/save overhead can outweigh the benefit. See the [current cache guards](docs/spec/rules.md#bun-dependency-cache-variant) and [a measured example](docs/measurements/2026-10-25-cache-review.md). The npm example below demonstrates one supported shape.\n\n## Install and upgrade\n\nThe CLI requires Node `^22.19.0 || >=24.0.0`. The plugin supports DSH `>=0.2.1-rc.2 <0.3.0-0` and `>=0.2.2-rc.1 <0.3.0-0`. Version `0.3.1` was tested against DSH `0.2.1-rc.2`; DSH `0.3.0` is not supported.\n\n```\nnpm install --global dsh-ci-diet@0.5.1\nci-diet --version\n```\n\nWithout a global install, replace the `ci-diet` command name with `npx dsh-ci-diet@0.5.1`, for example `npx dsh-ci-diet@0.5.1 report --cwd .`.\n\n```\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-ci-diet@0.5.1\ndsh --profile web\n```\n\nInstalling registers the plugin tools, the Settings page, and the **Settings → CI Diet Reports** review screen. Preflight, network access, and local apply are on by default for the plugin. Installation and startup do not call `gh`, collect history, run a scan, or modify a workflow.\n\n```\nnpm install --global dsh-ci-diet@latest\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-ci-diet@latest\n```\n\nRestart DSH after updating the plugin. Use `dsh plugin --profile web list`, `ci-diet --version`, or `npx dsh-ci-diet@latest --version` to verify the installed versions.\n\n## First scan and history report\n\nRun these commands from the repository you want to inspect. `--cwd .` means that repository; `--cwd` accepts another path, and relative paths resolve from the effective working directory. The first command is offline. History collection is a separate, explicit network opt-in.\n\n```\nci-diet scan --cwd .\ngh auth status\nci-diet sync --cwd . --network\nci-diet report --cwd .\nci-diet report --cwd . --format html --out report.html\n```\n\n`scan` prints a static report without network access; `--json` or `--out FILE` writes that output, but CLI scan does not save a report in the state store. `report` needs a saved report from CLI `sync`, plugin `ci_diet_scan`, or plugin `ci_diet_sync`. In this CLI-only sequence, sync stores the report; the HTML option then writes one self-contained file. History sync needs `gh` installed, authenticated, and able to read the repository’s Actions runs and jobs. `sync --network` is the CLI opt-in. It never needs GitHub write permission. A partial history still produces and stores a report, marking incomplete coverage. The plugin’s offline `ci_diet_scan` does save its report, so `ci_diet_report` can follow it directly.\n\nFor the DSH plugin, network access is enabled by default, so `ci_diet_sync` can run once `gh` is installed and authenticated. The switch only permits that tool to call `gh`; installation, startup, and Settings saves do not collect history by themselves. To block plugin network use, turn off **Allow network access** in **Settings → CI Diet** and choose **Save changes**. The page setting applies to plugin tools; it does not enable the CLI’s `--network` flag. Static scan and report work without network. The Settings page does not run an optimization by itself.\n\nA useful chat request makes the sequence and review boundary explicit. Replace the example absolute path with your own repository:\n\n> Run `ci_diet_scan` with cwd `C:\\work\\my-repo`, then `ci_diet_sync` for that same cwd and `ci_diet_report`. If `gh` is not authenticated or I turn off network access, stop after the scan. If you preview a patch with `ci_diet_plan`, show the edits only. Do not approve, apply, revert, commit, push, or deploy anything.\n\nThe plugin preview does not save a plan. Its `nextCommand` re-creates the plan through the CLI so that the plan is durable and can enter the human approval flow.\n\n## Offline npm cache plan (CD006)\n\nCD006 needs no run history. It matches exactly one setup-node v3–v7 and an unconditional `npm ci` or `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, with a prior checkout and tracked package manifest/lockfile. Literal step/job/workflow working directories are supported. pnpm must be installed by a prior `pnpm/action-setup`. The plan adds only `cache` and `cache-dependency-path`; installs and tests still run. Existing cache inputs and `package-manager-cache` opt-outs are preserved, and modern setup-node automatic caching is excluded. SHA-pinned setup-node and dynamic/mixed installs remain review-only (no automatic patch).\n\n```\nci-diet plan --cwd . --rule CD006 --workflow .github/workflows/ci.yml --job test --step 1\nci-diet plans --cwd . --plan PLAN_ID\n```\n\n`--step` is the zero-based index of the setup-node step; this example assumes checkout is step 0 and setup-node is step 1. CLI `plan` performs this static scan in memory and saves the plan without a prior `sync`; it leaves the latest saved report untouched. The plugin `ci_diet_plan` still needs a saved report, so run `ci_diet_scan` first. Approve and apply through the existing commands below. The plan and its attestation are saved during planning; no workflow file changes until a person approves the plan and runs apply.\n\n## CLI command reference\n\n```\nci-diet scan --cwd .\nci-diet sync --cwd . --network\nci-diet sync --cwd . --network --repo OWNER/REPO --days 7\nci-diet report --cwd .\nci-diet report --cwd . --format json\nci-diet report --cwd . --format html --out report.html\nci-diet diagnose --cwd .\nci-diet prune\nci-diet changes --cwd .\nci-diet plans --cwd . --plan PLAN_ID\nci-diet report --cwd . --lang ko\n```\n\n`scan` checks workflow files. `sync` reads history only after `--network`; `--repo` selects `OWNER/REPO` explicitly and `--days` adjusts the lookback within its configured bounds. `report` renders text, JSON, or HTML and writes `--out` relative to `--cwd`. `diagnose` explains job-name matching and coverage from stored history; add `--require-complete` to exit `3` for incomplete data. `prune` removes expired reports, plans, and cache entries under the state store settings. `measure --change <id> --before-runs <ids> --after-runs <ids> --network` links selected actual runs to an applied change using exact workflow hashes and reports runner-time differences plus success/rerun counts; see [measurement limits](docs/guide/plugin.md#measuring-an-applied-change). `changes` lists applied changes; `plans` reopens a saved plan. `--config FILE` merges a partial JSON configuration for any command.\n\n## Review, approve, apply, and revert\n\nA successful CLI `plan` prints the proposed diff, a real plan id such as `p_...`, and a confirmation made from the last 12 characters of the plan digest. Plan creation refuses stale evidence and other unsafe writes; a missing workflow can be a usage error with exit `1`. If a saved plan is viewed after its workspace or workflow disappears, `plans --plan` hides the diff, preserves the plan JSON, asks for a replan, and exits `3`. The same occurs when the workflow bytes no longer match the saved source hash. Inspect the diff and the plan again before approving.\n\n```\nci-diet plan --cwd . --rule CD001 --workflow .github/workflows/ci.yml --claims ci-only,replace-safe\nci-diet plans --cwd . --plan PLAN_ID\nci-diet approve --cwd . --plan PLAN_ID --confirm CONFIRMATION\nci-diet apply --cwd . --plan PLAN_ID\nci-diet revert --cwd . --change CHANGE_ID\n```\n\nReplace `PLAN_ID` with the id printed by the plan, `CONFIRMATION` with its 12-character digest tail, and `CHANGE_ID` with the id printed by apply. Every value is a literal argument; do not type angle brackets. `approve` creates a single-use approval, `apply` rewrites only the planned byte range in one workflow file, and `revert` restores that change’s backup. Review the resulting diff and run the repository’s checks as needed. CI Diet does not commit, push, deploy, run workflows, change branch protection, or delete artifacts.\n\nFor eligible PR-only CI, the CD001 example uses `ci-only` and `replace-safe` as human attestations. They state the operator’s review of cancellation semantics; they are not bypass switches. CD005 needs a measured `--job` and `--minutes`, and CD008 needs `--job`, a zero-based numeric `--step` array index for the target step, and artifact claims. CD006 needs `--job` and the zero-based `--step` index of the setup-node/setup-bun step; it has no claims. In both step rules, the numeric step is an array index, not a step-name token.\n\n## State and limitations\n\nThe CLI and plugin share the default state directory: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\CI-Diet\\profiles\\default` on Windows, otherwise `~/.local/state/ci-diet/profiles/default`. A plugin `stateDir` override is a separate store; pass the same absolute path to the CLI with `--state-dir` on `plan`, `approve`, `apply`, and `revert`. Relative CLI `--state-dir` paths resolve against the effective `--cwd`. Existing state is never migrated automatically between directories.\n\nThe Web client has Settings and the **CI Diet Reports** review screen. Report, approve, apply, and revert controls passed a real-browser E2E check in an earlier commit. The defaults migration was verified separately in a DSH `0.2.1-rc.2` runtime with configEditor, SettingsForms, and Loader in a temporary profile: legacy `false` values were saved as `true`, and a later explicit `false` survived restart. That runtime check was not a new browser render. Approval and apply reach the host from that screen, and `localApplyEnabled` is on by default. No plugin tool performs approval or application. A plan edits one existing workflow file at byte ranges and refuses unsupported structures. Findings can be wrong or incomplete when history or workflow attribution is partial, and another system may have more accurate billing data. Use the report as review evidence, then verify the effect in GitHub.\n\n## Cost and evidence\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| `observedRunnerSeconds` | Runner time recorded by collected runs |\n| `modeledRoundedMinutes` | Per-job minutes rounded up for modeling |\n| `listPriceUsd` | Cost at the embedded list-price snapshot |\n| `actualBilledUsd` | Always `null` until the actual bill can be proven |\n\nReports embed the pricing snapshot and a content hash so numbers can be reproduced. They do not claim automatic savings. The HTML report has inline CSS, no scripts, and no external requests.\n\n## Languages\n\nThe DSH Settings UI, CLI messages, HTML reports, and these six READMEs support English, Korean, Simplified Chinese, Hindi, Spanish, and French. The detailed specifications remain English. Selection order is `--lang`, the DSH locale, `LC_ALL`/`LC_MESSAGES`/`LANG`, then English. The CLI language codes are `en`, `ko`, `zh-Hans`, `hi`, `es`, and `fr`; replace `ko` in the example command with the desired code. Regional tags resolve by language. Reports are stored in English and localized when displayed. Rule ids, error codes, enum values, paths, hashes, and numbers stay literal. The HTML `lang` attribute follows the selected locale. DSH tool descriptions are captured at plugin load, so reload after changing the DSH language preference.\n\n## Development\n\n```\nbun install\nnode scripts/test-core.mjs\nnode scripts/gen-types.mjs --check\nnode scripts/sync-contracts.mjs --check\nbun run typecheck\nbun run lint\nbun run test:docs\n```\n\nRun tests with Node so published entry points stay Node-compatible. Bun is used for dependency management.\n\n## Release\n\nPushing a tag that matches `package.json` starts `.github/workflows/publish.yml`. In the following commands, replace the literal `VERSION` in both arguments with a new version; version `0.3.1` is already published, so do not create that tag again.\n\n```\ngit tag vVERSION\ngit push origin vVERSION\n```\n\nThe workflow compares the tag with `package.json`, runs the release checks, refuses an existing npm version, and publishes with npm trusted publishing through GitHub OIDC. The trusted publisher must name `publish.yml`.\n\n## Layout\n\n```\nsrc/core        workflow parsing, rules, savings, patch engine\nsrc/adapters    GitHub, git, storage\nsrc/client      Web Settings and review UI\nsrc/dsh         host plugin and bundle code\nsrc/cli         command-line entry\nsrc/shared      i18n and shared helpers\ncontracts       JSON Schemas from the frozen design pack\nexamples        sample records and evaluation vectors\ndocs/spec       normative specification\nscripts         contract and documentation checks\ntests/unit      fast checks that need no network\n```\n\n## Documentation\n\nThe detailed specification, rule, cost, patch, storage, and decision documents are English. The specification index is [docs/spec/README.md](docs/spec/README.md). Also available: [rules](docs/spec/rules.md), [cost model](docs/spec/cost-model.md), [patch model](docs/spec/patch-model.md), [storage and errors](docs/spec/storage.md), [decisions](docs/spec/decisions.md), [measurement](docs/spikes/a0a-rules.md), the [plugin and CLI guide](docs/guide/plugin.md), and [contract provenance](contracts/UPSTREAM.md).\n\n## License\n\nMIT\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "package.json",
      "content": "{\n  \"name\": \"dsh-ci-diet\",\n  \"version\": \"0.5.1\",\n  \"description\": \"Find wasted GitHub Actions runner time and propose small, reviewable local patches.\",\n  \"keywords\": [\n    \"dsh-plugin\",\n    \"github-actions\",\n    \"ci\",\n    \"cost-optimization\",\n    \"workflow\"\n  ],\n  \"homepage\": \"https://github.com/0disoft/dsh-ci-diet#readme\",\n  \"bugs\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/0disoft/dsh-ci-diet/issues\"\n  },\n  \"repository\": {\n    \"type\": \"git\",\n    \"url\": \"git+https://github.com/0disoft/dsh-ci-diet.git\"\n  },\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"bin\": {\n    \"ci-diet\": \"./dist/cli/index.js\"\n  },\n  \"exports\": {\n    \".\": \"./dist/dsh/bootstrap.js\",\n    \"./client\": {\n      \"types\": \"./client/index.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./client/index.js\"\n    },\n    \"./package.json\": \"./package.json\"\n  },\n  \"files\": [\n    \"dist\",\n    \"client\",\n    \"cordis.patch.yml\",\n    \"README*.md\",\n    \"LICENSE\"\n  ],\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \"^22.19.0 || >=24.0.0\",\n    \"dsh\": \">=0.2.1-rc.2 <0.3.0-0 || >=0.2.2-rc.1 <0.3.0-0\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit\",\n    \"lint\": \"oxlint src tests\",\n    \"format\": \"oxfmt src tests\",\n    \"gen:types\": \"node scripts/gen-types.mjs\",\n    \"check:types\": \"node scripts/gen-types.mjs --check\",\n    \"gen:data\": \"node scripts/gen-data.mjs\",\n    \"check:data\": \"node scripts/gen-data.mjs --check\",\n    \"test:core\": \"node scripts/test-core.mjs\",\n    \"build\": \"tsc -p tsconfig.build.json && node scripts/build-client.mjs\",\n    \"build:client\": \"node scripts/build-client.mjs\",\n    \"prepack\": \"npm run build\",\n    \"smoke:node\": \"node dist/cli/index.js --version\",\n    \"check:contracts\": \"node scripts/sync-contracts.mjs --check\",\n    \"test:docs\": \"node scripts/check-docs.mjs\",\n    \"test:plugin\": \"node --test tests/unit/dsh-plugin.test.ts\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"ajv\": \"^8.17.1\",\n    \"ajv-formats\": \"^3.0.1\",\n    \"yaml\": \"^2.8.1\"\n  },\n  \"peerDependenciesMeta\": {\n    \"@deepseek-ai/cordis\": {\n      \"optional\": true\n    },\n    \"@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools\": {\n      \"optional\": true\n    }\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@deepseek-ai/cordis\": \"4.0.5\",\n    \"@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools\": \"0.2.1-rc.2\",\n    \"@deepseek-ai/schemastery\": \"3.18.5\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"^24.0.0\",\n    \"oxfmt\": \"^0.74.0\",\n    \"oxlint\": \"^1.89.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.9.0\"\n  },\n  \"peerDependencies\": {\n    \"@deepseek-ai/cordis\": \"^4.0.5\",\n    \"@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools\": \">=0.2.1-rc.2 <0.3.0-0 || >=0.2.2-rc.1 <0.3.0-0\",\n    \"@deepseek-ai/schemastery\": \"^3.18.5\"\n  },\n  \"main\": \"./dist/dsh/bootstrap.js\",\n  \"dsh\": {\n    \"bundle\": {\n      \"patch\": \"./cordis.patch.yml\"\n    },\n    \"client\": {\n      \"platform\": \"web\",\n      \"inject\": [\n        \"@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-settings\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/dsh/host/preflight.ts",
      "content": "import { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { isAbsolute, join, resolve } from \"node:path\";\nimport { existsSync, readdirSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport type { Context } from \"@deepseek-ai/cordis\";\nimport type { PreToolDecision, ToolExecution } from \"@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools\";\nimport { digestOf } from \"../../shared/cdj1.ts\";\nimport { discoverWorkflows } from \"../../core/scan/discover.ts\";\nimport { parseWorkflow } from \"../../core/workflow/parse.ts\";\nimport { npmCacheDependencies, downloadCacheTargets } from \"../../core/rules/npm-cache.ts\";\nimport type { RuleId } from \"../../core/model/domain.ts\";\n\n/** Only literal commands; substitutions, heredocs, pipelines and script wrappers stay untouched. */\nfunction commands(source: string): string[][] | null {\n  if (source.length > 16_384) return null;\n  const out: string[][] = [];\n  let words: string[] = [], word = \"\", quote = \"\";\n  const flushWord = () => { if (word !== \"\") { words.push(word); word = \"\"; } };\n  const flush = () => { flushWord(); if (words.length > 0) out.push(words); words = []; };\n  for (let i = 0; i < source.length; i += 1) {\n    const ch = source[i]!;\n    if (quote !== \"\") {\n      if (ch === quote) { quote = \"\"; continue; }\n      if ((quote === '\"' && /[$`\\\\]/.test(ch)) || ch === \"\\n\") return null;\n      word += ch; continue;\n    }\n    if (ch === \"'\" || ch === '\"') { quote = ch; continue; }\n    if (ch === \"#\" && word === \"\") { while (i < source.length && source[i] !== \"\\n\") i += 1; flush(); continue; }\n    if (/[$`\\\\<>|(){}]/.test(ch)) return null;\n    if (ch === \"&\") { if (source[++i] !== \"&\") return null; flush(); continue; }\n    if (ch === \";\" || ch === \"\\n\") { if (words[0] === \"cd\") return null; flush(); continue; }\n    if (/\\s/.test(ch)) { flushWord(); continue; }\n    word += ch;\n  }\n  if (quote !== \"\") return null;\n  flush(); return out;\n}\n\n/** Resolve explicit cd / git -C before a recognized publish command, without executing shell text. */\nexport function deploymentDirectories(command: string, cwd: string): string[] {\n  const parsed = commands(command);\n  if (parsed === null) return [];\n  let current = cwd;\n  const roots = new Set<string>();\n  for (const words of parsed) {\n    const [head, verb] = words;\n    if (head === \"cd\") {\n      if (words.length !== 2 || verb === \"-\" || verb === \"~\") return [];\n      current = resolve(current, verb!); continue;\n    }\n    let args = words;\n    let root = current;\n    if (head === \"git\" && verb === \"-C\") {\n      if (words[2] === undefined) return [];\n      root = resolve(current, words[2]); args = [\"git\", ...words.slice(3)];\n    }\n    const publish = args[0] === \"git\" && args[1] === \"push\"\n      || [\"npm\", \"pnpm\", \"bun\"].includes(args[0] ?? \"\") && args[1] === \"publish\"\n      || args[0] === \"yarn\" && (args[1] === \"publish\" || args[1] === \"npm\" && args[2] === \"publish\")\n      || args[0] === \"wrangler\" && args[1] === \"deploy\"\n      || args[0] === \"npx\" && args[1] === \"wrangler\" && args[2] === \"deploy\"\n      || [\"npm\", \"pnpm\", \"bun\"].includes(args[0] ?? \"\") && args[1] === \"run\" && args[2] === \"deploy\";\n    if (publish && !args.some((a) => [\"--dry-run\", \"-n\", \"--help\", \"-h\", \"--version\"].includes(a))) roots.add(root);\n    // A preceding arbitrary command could change directory or replace the workflow.\n    // Do not pretend that an inspection before that command covers its output.\n    if (!publish && head !== \"git\") return [];\n    if (head === \"git\" && !publish && ![\"status\", \"diff\", \"log\", \"add\", \"commit\"].includes(verb ?? \"\")) return [];\n  }\n  return roots.size <= 4 ? [...roots] : [];\n}\n\nexport interface PreflightSettings {\n  readonly enabled: boolean;\n  readonly rules: readonly RuleId[];\n  readonly maxWorkflowBytes: number;\n}\n\ninterface Opportunity {\n  readonly rule: string;\n  readonly workflow: string;\n  readonly job?: string;\n  readonly step?: number;\n  readonly next: string;\n}\n\nexport function inspectPreflight(cwd: string, settings: PreflightSettings) {\n  const root = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"rev-parse\", \"--show-toplevel\"], { cwd, encoding: \"utf8\", windowsHide: true, timeout: 2000, stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"] }).trim();\n  const directory = join(root, \".github\", \"workflows\");\n  if (existsSync(directory) && readdirSync(directory).length > 32) throw new Error(\"preflight workflow budget exceeded\");\n  const discovery = discoverWorkflows(root, { maxBytes: Math.min(settings.maxWorkflowBytes || 524288, 524288) });\n  if (discovery.workflows.reduce((total, file) => total + file.bytes, 0) > 2 * 1024 * 1024) throw new Error(\"preflight byte budget exceeded\");\n  const workflows = discovery.workflows.map((file) => parseWorkflow(file.path, file.text));\n  const opportunities: Opportunity[] = [];\n  const cacheTargets = settings.rules.includes(\"CD006\") ? workflows.flatMap((workflow) => downloadCacheTargets(workflow, root).map((t) => ({ workflow, ...t }))) : [];\n  const dependencies = cacheTargets.map((target) => npmCacheDependencies(root, target));\n  for (const [index, { workflow, job, step }] of cacheTargets.entries()) if (dependencies[index] !== null) opportunities.push({ rule: \"CD006\", workflow: workflow.path,\n    job: job.key, step: step.index, next: \"ci_diet_scan then ci_diet_plan for this cwd, job and step; review and get human approval before apply\" });\n  if (settings.rules.includes(\"CD006\")) for (const w of workflows) {\n    if (w.parseError !== null || w.unsupported.length > 0) continue;\n    for (const job of w.jobs) {\n      if (cacheTargets.some((t) => t.workflow.path === w.path && t.job.key === job.key)) continue;\n      if (!job.steps.some((s) => s.uses?.startsWith(\"oven-sh/setup-bun@\"))\n        || job.steps.some((s) => s.uses !== null && (/cache/i.test(s.uses) || s.uses.startsWith(\"./\")))) continue;\n      if (job.steps.some((s) => s.run?.trim() === \"bun install --frozen-lockfile\")) opportunities.push({ rule: \"BUN_CACHE_REVIEW\", workflow: w.path, job: job.key,\n        next: \"No explicit dependency cache step found. Review Bun cache configuration and consider caching dependency downloads with an OS/Bun-version/lockfile key before install. Keep frozen install and tests. This is advice, not a CD006 plan; no measured savings.\" });\n    }\n  }\n  if (settings.rules.includes(\"CD001\")) for (const w of workflows) {\n    if (w.parseError !== null || w.unsupported.length > 0 || w.concurrency !== null || w.triggers.length !== 1 || w.triggers[0] !== \"pull_request\") continue;\n    opportunities.push({ rule: \"CD001\", workflow: w.path, next: \"Review whether superseded PR runs can be cancelled; ci_diet_sync requires network opt-in and plan requires human ci-only/replace-safe claims\" });\n  }\n  return { root, opportunities, fingerprint: digestOf({ workflows: workflows.map((w) => [w.path, w.sha256]), dependencies, rules: settings.rules }) };\n}\n\n/** A once-per-session/source reminder, never an automatic patch or network request. */\nexport function registerPreflight(ctx: Context, settings: () => PreflightSettings, notice: () => string): void {\n  const seen = new WeakMap<object, Map<string, string>>();\n  ctx.on(\"tools/pre-execute\", async (exec: ToolExecution, next: () => Promise<PreToolDecision>) => {\n    const decision = await next();\n    if (decision.kind !== \"allow\" || exec.name !== \"bash\" || exec.agent === undefined || exec.signal.aborted) return decision;\n    const args = exec.arguments as { command?: unknown; workdir?: unknown } | null;\n    if (typeof args?.command !== \"string\") return decision;\n    // Only the stateless bash contract is supported. Persistent bash may have\n    // changed its own cwd, which the session directory cannot establish.\n    const definition = ctx.tools.get(\"bash\", exec.agent);\n    const parameters = definition?.parameters as { properties?: Record<string, unknown> } | undefined;\n    if (parameters?.properties?.workdir === undefined) return decision;\n    try {\n      const config = settings();\n      if (!config.enabled) return decision;\n      const service = ctx.get(\"workingDirectory\") as { get(session: unknown): string } | undefined;\n      const base = service?.get(exec.agent.session);\n      const cwd = typeof args.workdir === \"string\" && isAbsolute(args.workdir) ? args.workdir\n        : base === undefined ? null : resolve(base, typeof args.workdir === \"string\" ? args.workdir : \".\");\n      if (cwd === null) return decision;\n      const notices = [];\n      const previous = new Map(seen.get(exec.agent));\n      for (const directory of deploymentDirectories(args.command, cwd)) {\n        const report = inspectPreflight(directory, config);\n        if (report.opportunities.length === 0 || previous.get(report.root) === report.fingerprint) continue;\n        if (previous.size >= 64) previous.delete(previous.keys().next().value!);\n        previous.set(report.root, report.fingerprint);\n        notices.push({ cwd: report.root, opportunities: report.opportunities.slice(0, 8), total: report.opportunities.length });\n      }\n      if (exec.signal.aborted || notices.length === 0) return decision;\n      seen.set(exec.agent, previous);\n      return { kind: \"deny\", reason: notice() + \"\\n\" + JSON.stringify(notices) };\n    } catch {\n      // Advisory inspection must never lock users out of deploying.\n      return decision;\n    }\n  });\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/core/patch/approval.ts",
      "content": "import type { PatchPlan } from \"../contracts/schema.ts\";\nimport type { ApprovalNonce, PatchStore } from \"./store.ts\";\nimport { digestOf } from \"../../shared/cdj1.ts\";\nimport { acquireStoreLock } from \"./apply.ts\";\nimport type { Clock, IdSource } from \"../support/clock.ts\";\nimport { APPROVE_LOCK_WAIT_MS, DEFAULT_APPROVAL_TTL_SECONDS } from \"../policy/constants.ts\";\n\nexport interface ApproveInput {\n  readonly store: PatchStore;\n  readonly planId: string;\n  readonly confirmation: string;\n  readonly subjectId: string;\n  readonly channel: \"human-ui\" | \"human-cli\";\n  readonly now: Date;\n  readonly approvalTtlSeconds?: number;\n  /** Optional time source for lock bookkeeping; defaults to the system clock. */\n  readonly clock?: Clock;\n  /** Optional id source for lock tokens; defaults to crypto.randomUUID. */\n  readonly ids?: IdSource;\n}\n\nexport interface ApproveResult {\n  readonly plan: PatchPlan;\n  readonly nonce: ApprovalNonce;\n  readonly warnings?: readonly string[];\n}\n\n/** The human must type the last 12 hex characters of the plan digest. */\nexport function approvalConfirmation(plan: PatchPlan): string {\n  return plan.planDigest.slice(-12);\n}\n\nexport function approvePlan(input: ApproveInput): ApproveResult {\n  // Read once to validate the id through the store before it names a lock path.\n  const initial = input.store.readPlan(input.planId);\n  if (initial === null) throw new Error(\"PLAN_NOT_FOUND: \" + input.planId);\n  // The approval is a two-step write (nonce, then plan status). Serialize it per\n  // plan so concurrent approvers cannot leave a nonce without its status, or a\n  // status pointing at a nonce that a second approval overwrote.\n  const lock = acquireStoreLock(input.store, \"approve-\" + initial.plan.planId, APPROVE_LOCK_WAIT_MS, { clock: input.clock, ids: input.ids });\n  try {\n    return approveLocked(input);\n  } finally {\n    lock.release();\n  }\n}\n\nfunction approveLocked(input: ApproveInput): ApproveResult {\n  const stored = input.store.readPlan(input.planId);\n  if (stored === null) throw new Error(\"PLAN_NOT_FOUND: \" + input.planId);\n  const plan = stored.plan;\n  const previous = input.store.readNonce(plan.planId);\n  if (input.store.listChanges().some((change) => change.planId === plan.planId && change.state !== \"NOT_APPLIED\")) {\n    throw new Error(\"PLAN_ALREADY_USED: \" + input.planId);\n  }\n  if (plan.status.state === \"approved\") {\n    if (previous === null || previous.nonceId !== plan.status.approvalNonceId || previous.planDigest !== plan.planDigest) {\n      throw new Error(\"NONCE_INVALID: approval record missing or mismatched\");\n    }\n    const until = Date.parse(previous.createdAt) + (input.approvalTtlSeconds ?? DEFAULT_APPROVAL_TTL_SECONDS) * 1000;\n    if (!Number.isFinite(until) || input.now.getTime() < until) throw new Error(\"PLAN_ALREADY_APPROVED: \" + input.planId);\n  }\n  if (input.now.getTime() >= Date.parse(plan.payload.expiresAt)) throw new Error(\"PLAN_EXPIRED: \" + plan.payload.expiresAt);\n  if (input.confirmation.trim() !== approvalConfirmation(plan)) throw new Error(\"NONCE_INVALID: confirmation does not match the plan digest\");\n  const at = input.now.toISOString().replace(/\\.\\d{3}Z$/, \"Z\");\n  const nonce: ApprovalNonce = {\n    nonceId: \"n_\" + digestOf({ planId: plan.planId, digest: plan.planDigest, at }).slice(\"sha256:\".length, \"sha256:\".length + 24),\n    planDigest: plan.planDigest,\n    createdAt: at,\n    subjectId: input.subjectId,\n    channel: input.channel,\n  };\n  const approved: PatchPlan = {\n    ...plan,\n    status: {\n      state: \"approved\",\n      revision: plan.status.revision + 1,\n      previewedAt: plan.status.previewedAt ?? at,\n      approvedAt: at,\n      approvalNonceId: nonce.nonceId,\n    },\n  };\n  // A failed nonce write must leave the plan available for an explicit approval retry.\n  input.store.saveNonce(plan.planId, nonce);\n  try {\n    input.store.updatePlanStatus(plan.planId, approved.status, plan.status.revision);\n  } catch (error) {\n    // Do not leave a nonce that names a status this approval never published.\n    if (previous !== null) input.store.saveNonce(plan.planId, previous);\n    else input.store.consumeNonce(plan.planId, nonce.nonceId);\n    throw error;\n  }\n  const warnings = input.store.appendSummaryEvent({ type: \"approved\", planId: plan.planId, nonceId: nonce.nonceId, channel: input.channel }, input.now);\n  return { plan: approved, nonce, ...(warnings.length > 0 ? { warnings } : {}) };\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/core/patch/verify.ts",
      "content": "import { digestOf, sha256Hex } from \"../../shared/cdj1.ts\";\nimport type { Attestation, PatchPlan, PolicySnapshot } from \"../contracts/schema.ts\";\nimport { attestationSatisfiesRule, isPatchRule } from \"./eligibility.ts\";\nimport { isExpired, isStale } from \"../support/clock.ts\";\nimport type { PatchRule } from \"./eligibility.ts\";\nimport { POLICY_MAX_AGE_MS } from \"../policy/constants.ts\";\n\nexport { POLICY_MAX_AGE_MS } from \"../policy/constants.ts\";\n\nexport type ApplyReasonCode =\n  | \"PLAN_DIGEST_MISMATCH\"\n  | \"SYNTHETIC_PLAN\"\n  | \"PLAN_EXPIRED\"\n  | \"ATTESTATION_MISSING\"\n  | \"ATTESTATION_EXPIRED\"\n  | \"ATTESTATION_REVOKED\"\n  | \"ATTESTATION_HASH_MISMATCH\"\n  | \"ATTESTATION_SCOPE_INSUFFICIENT\"\n  | \"ATTESTATION_CLAIMS_INSUFFICIENT\"\n  | \"EDIT_OUT_OF_SCOPE\"\n  | \"DEPENDENCY_HASH_MISMATCH\"\n  | \"BLOCKERS_PRESENT\"\n  | \"RULE_NOT_ALLOWED\"\n  | \"COVERAGE_INSUFFICIENT_FOR_WRITE\"\n  | \"SOURCE_HASH_MISMATCH\"\n  | \"NONCE_INVALID\"\n  | \"POLICY_STALE\"\n  | \"BACKUP_UNAVAILABLE\";\n\nexport interface ApplyCheckInput {\n  readonly plan: PatchPlan;\n  readonly now: Date;\n  readonly currentText: string;\n  readonly currentDependencyHash: string;\n  readonly coverageWriteAllowed: boolean;\n  readonly nonceValid: boolean;\n  readonly backupAvailable: boolean;\n  /** Attestations re-read from the store, so a revocation after approval is visible. */\n  readonly attestations?: readonly Attestation[];\n  /** Policy snapshots rebuilt from the current history cache. */\n  readonly currentPolicies?: readonly PolicySnapshot[];\n  /** Overrides the shared policy freshness bound; defaults to 600 000 ms. */\n  readonly policyMaxAgeMs?: number;\n}\n\ntype PolicyKind = PolicySnapshot[\"kind\"];\n\n/** Policy kinds a plan must carry for the rules it edits. */\nexport function requiredPolicyKinds(ruleIds: readonly string[]): PolicyKind[] {\n  const kinds = new Set<PolicyKind>();\n  for (const ruleId of ruleIds) {\n    if (ruleId === \"CD001\") kinds.add(\"protection\");\n    if (ruleId === \"CD008\") kinds.add(\"retention\");\n  }\n  return [...kinds].sort();\n}\n\nfunction isoMillis(value: string): number {\n  return Date.parse(value);\n}\n\nfunction scopeCovers(attestation: Attestation, plan: PatchPlan): boolean {\n  if (attestation.bindingId !== plan.payload.bindingId) return false;\n  if (attestation.workflowPath !== plan.payload.workflowPath) return false;\n  for (const edit of plan.payload.edits) {\n    if (edit.ruleId === \"CD001\") {\n      if (attestation.scope !== \"workflow\") return false;\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (attestation.scope === \"workflow\") return false;\n    const jobKey = /^jobs\\.([^.]+)\\./.exec(edit.semanticPath)?.[1];\n    if (jobKey === undefined || attestation.jobKey !== jobKey) return false;\n    if (edit.ruleId === \"CD008\" || edit.ruleId === \"CD006\") {\n      const stepIndex = /^jobs\\.[^.]+\\.steps\\[(\\d+)\\]/.exec(edit.semanticPath)?.[1];\n      if (stepIndex === undefined) return false;\n      const expectedStepKey = \"steps[\" + stepIndex + \"]\";\n      if (attestation.scope === \"step\" && attestation.stepKey !== expectedStepKey) return false;\n    }\n  }\n  return true;\n}\n\nfunction validAttestations(input: ApplyCheckInput): { readonly valid: Attestation[]; readonly reasons: ApplyReasonCode[] } {\n  const reasons: ApplyReasonCode[] = [];\n  const payload = input.plan.payload;\n  const now = input.now.getTime();\n  const attestations = input.attestations ?? payload.attestations;\n  if (attestations.length === 0) return { valid: [], reasons: [\"ATTESTATION_MISSING\"] };\n  const valid: Attestation[] = [];\n  let sawExpired = false;\n  let sawRevoked = false;\n  let sawMismatch = false;\n  for (const attestation of attestations) {\n    if (attestation.revokedAt !== null) {\n      sawRevoked = true;\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (isExpired(now, isoMillis(attestation.expiresAt))) {\n      sawExpired = true;\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (attestation.workflowHash !== payload.sourceHash || attestation.dependencyHash !== payload.dependencyHash) {\n      sawMismatch = true;\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (!scopeCovers(attestation, input.plan)) continue;\n    valid.push(attestation);\n  }\n  if (valid.length === 0) {\n    if (sawMismatch) reasons.push(\"ATTESTATION_HASH_MISMATCH\");\n    else if (sawRevoked) reasons.push(\"ATTESTATION_REVOKED\");\n    else if (sawExpired) reasons.push(\"ATTESTATION_EXPIRED\");\n    else if (attestations.some((attestation) => attestation.bindingId === payload.bindingId)) reasons.push(\"ATTESTATION_SCOPE_INSUFFICIENT\");\n    else reasons.push(\"ATTESTATION_MISSING\");\n  }\n  return { valid, reasons };\n}\n\n/** Return the closed list of failed apply invariants, in contract order. */\nexport function checkApply(input: ApplyCheckInput): ApplyReasonCode[] {\n  const reasons: ApplyReasonCode[] = [];\n  const now = input.now.getTime();\n  const payload = input.plan.payload;\n\n  if (digestOf(payload) !== input.plan.planDigest) reasons.push(\"PLAN_DIGEST_MISMATCH\");\n  // A matching digest proves unchanged bytes, not that the rule summary names\n  // the actual edits. Policy selection and allowedRules must not trust a\n  // different rule set, including in previously saved/externally built plans.\n  const editedRules = new Set(payload.edits.map((edit) => edit.ruleId));\n  const declaredRules = new Set(payload.ruleIds);\n  if (editedRules.size !== declaredRules.size || declaredRules.size !== payload.ruleIds.length\n    || payload.ruleIds.some((rule) => !editedRules.has(rule))) reasons.push(\"RULE_NOT_ALLOWED\");\n  if (input.plan.provenance !== \"observed\") reasons.push(\"SYNTHETIC_PLAN\");\n  if (isExpired(now, isoMillis(payload.expiresAt))) reasons.push(\"PLAN_EXPIRED\");\n\n  const attestationCheck = validAttestations(input);\n  reasons.push(...attestationCheck.reasons);\n  if (attestationCheck.valid.length > 0) {\n    for (const edit of payload.edits) {\n      if (!isPatchRule(edit.ruleId)) continue;\n      const rule: PatchRule = edit.ruleId;\n      if (!attestationCheck.valid.some((attestation) => attestationSatisfiesRule(rule, attestation.claims))) {\n        reasons.push(\"ATTESTATION_CLAIMS_INSUFFICIENT\");\n        break;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (digestOf({ dependencies: payload.dependencies }) !== input.currentDependencyHash) reasons.push(\"DEPENDENCY_HASH_MISMATCH\");\n  if (payload.blockers.length > 0) reasons.push(\"BLOCKERS_PRESENT\");\n  if (!input.coverageWriteAllowed) reasons.push(\"COVERAGE_INSUFFICIENT_FOR_WRITE\");\n  const currentHash = \"sha256:\" + sha256Hex(input.currentText);\n  if (currentHash !== payload.sourceHash) reasons.push(\"SOURCE_HASH_MISMATCH\");\n  if (!input.nonceValid) reasons.push(\"NONCE_INVALID\");\n\n  for (const kind of requiredPolicyKinds(payload.ruleIds)) {\n    const planPolicy = payload.policies.find((policy) => policy.kind === kind);\n    if (planPolicy === undefined || planPolicy.status !== \"known\" || isStale(now, isoMillis(planPolicy.observedAt), input.policyMaxAgeMs ?? POLICY_MAX_AGE_MS)) {\n      reasons.push(\"POLICY_STALE\");\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (input.currentPolicies !== undefined) {\n      const current = input.currentPolicies.find((policy) => policy.kind === kind);\n      if (current === undefined || current.status !== \"known\" || current.policyHash !== planPolicy.policyHash\n        || isStale(now, isoMillis(current.observedAt), input.policyMaxAgeMs ?? POLICY_MAX_AGE_MS)) {\n        reasons.push(\"POLICY_STALE\");\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (!input.backupAvailable) reasons.push(\"BACKUP_UNAVAILABLE\");\n  return [...new Set(reasons)];\n}\n"
